# Conventional Commits

Spec: [conventionalcommits.org](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/)

## Format

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

## Type -> semver

| Type | When | Semver |
|---|---|---|
| `feat` | New feature | MINOR |
| `fix` | Bug fix | PATCH |
| `BREAKING CHANGE` | Breaking API/behavior change | MAJOR |

Other types (no semver bump): `build`, `chore`, `ci`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`.

## Rules

- `type(optional-scope)[optional !]: description` — imperative, lowercase, no period.
- `!` before colon marks breaking change: `feat(api)!: remove endpoint`.
- `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer required when `!` is used in header.
- `BREAKING CHANGE` must be uppercase; all other types are case-insensitive.

## Correct vs wrong

```
# CORRECT
feat(auth): add password reset email flow
fix(ui): correct empty-state spacing on settings
feat(api)!: require signed webhooks

BREAKING CHANGE: unsigned webhook requests are rejected.

# WRONG: vague, past tense, no type
updated some stuff
Fixed bug
WIP: changes
```